WEBVTT

00:05:57.695 --> 00:06:00.615
"high frequency stores," which is all these tiny kiosks

00:06:00.615 --> 00:06:03.926
and the lady in the canoe and all these other businesses

00:06:03.926 --> 00:06:09.273
that exist in System D, the informal economy,

00:06:09.273 --> 00:06:12.671
and Procter &amp; Gamble makes 20 percent of its money

00:06:12.671 --> 00:06:14.720
from that market segment,

00:06:14.720 --> 00:06:18.156
and it's the only market segment that's growing.

00:06:18.156 --> 00:06:21.264
So Procter &amp; Gamble says, "We don't care whether a store

00:06:21.264 --> 00:06:24.158
is incorporated or registered or anything like that.

00:06:24.158 --> 00:06:27.991
We want our products in that store."

00:06:27.991 --> 00:06:30.163
And then there's mobile phones.